# OCP (Open/Closed Principle)

> A class should be **open for extension but closed for modification.**

This means we should be able to add new functionality without changing existing, tested code.

---

### Example

In a payment system, instead of modifying the existing `PaymentService` whenever a new payment method is added, use a common `Payment` interface and implement it for `UPI`, `Credit Card`, etc.

This allows new payment methods to be added without modifying the existing payment service.
